openapi: "3.1.0"
x-mcp:
  transport: [ stdio, http ]
  orchestration: code
  endpoint_tools: hidden
info:
  title: Conduyt API
  version: "1.0.0"
  description: |
    The Conduyt CRM API provides programmatic access to your CRM data including
    contacts, companies, deals, pipelines, tasks, notes, automations, invoices,
    email sequences, and more.

    ## Authentication

    All authenticated endpoints require a Bearer token (API key) in the
    `Authorization` header:

    ```
    Authorization: Bearer cdy_<your-api-key>
    ```

    API keys are generated in **Settings > API Keys** within the Conduyt
    dashboard. Keys use the `cdy_` prefix and are hashed with bcrypt on
    creation — the full key is shown exactly once at creation time.

    Session cookie authentication (`conduyt_session`) is also supported for
    browser-based clients but is not recommended for integrations.

    ## Rate Limiting

    API keys enforce a per-key rate limit. New keys default to 100 requests per
    minute and can be configured at creation time or with PATCH `/api-keys/{id}`.
    Some public and provider-facing endpoints also enforce stricter per-IP or
    per-account limits. When exceeded, the API returns `429 Too Many Requests`
    with a `Retry-After` header indicating seconds until the next allowed
    request.

    | Endpoint Group      | Limit               |
    |---------------------|---------------------|
    | API keys            | Default 100 / min per key |
    | Login/reset         | 5 / min per IP      |
    | Registration        | 3 / hour per IP     |
    | Contact/Deal create | 30 / min per IP     |
    | Inbound messages    | 120 / min per account/IP |

    ## Pagination

    List endpoints support cursor-based pagination via query parameters:

    - `page` — Page number (default: 1)
    - `per_page` — Items per page (default: 50, max: 200)
    - `limit` — Accepted as an alias of `per_page` on `GET /contacts`; if both are
      sent they must carry the same value.

    A page size above the maximum, a non-integer, a value below 1, or a
    pagination key repeated with different values is rejected with `400`
    (the message names the parameter and the rule); nothing is silently
    clamped or ignored.

    Responses include a `meta` object: `{ page, per_page, total }`.

    An operation that documents its own pagination rules follows those instead.
    `GET /sms-providers/options` pages with an opaque `cursor` and a `limit`
    that is capped at 50 rather than rejected; its responses carry
    `meta: { nextCursor, truncated }`.

    ## Response Format

    All successful responses wrap data in a `data` envelope:
    ```json
    { "data": { ... } }
    ```

    Error responses use:
    ```json
    { "error": "Human-readable error message" }
    ```

    ## Multi-Tenancy

    Conduyt is multi-tenant. All data is scoped to the authenticated user's
    current account. API keys are bound to a specific account at creation time.

    ## Webhook Events

    Outbound webhooks fire on events including:
    `contact.created`, `contact.updated`, `contact.deleted`,
    `deal.created`, `deal.updated`, `deal.won`, `deal.lost`,
    `task.created`, `task.completed`, `note.created`,
    `appointment.created`, `appointment.updated`,
    `form.submitted`, `invoice.paid`

    Payloads are signed with HMAC-SHA256 using the webhook's secret. Retry
    schedule: 1m, 5m, 30m, 2h, 12h, 72h (7 total attempts including the initial delivery).
  contact:
    name: Conduyt Support
    url: https://conduyt.app
    email: support@conduyt.app
  license:
    name: Proprietary
    url: https://conduyt.app/terms

servers:
  - url: https://conduyt.app/api/v1
    description: Production

tags:
  - name: Auth
    description: Authentication, registration, password management
  - name: Contacts
    description: Contact management, tagging, scoring, import/export, merge, duplicates
  - name: Companies
    description: Company (organization) management
  - name: Deals
    description: Deal/opportunity management within pipelines
  - name: Pipelines
    description: Sales pipeline and stage management
  - name: Tasks
    description: Task management with assignment and due dates
  - name: Notes
    description: Notes attached to contacts or deals
  - name: Tags
    description: Tag management and merging
  - name: Activities
    description: Activity feed and logging
  - name: Messages
    description: SMS and email message history
  - name: Email
    description: Send individual and bulk emails
  - name: Email Templates
    description: Reusable email/SMS templates
  - name: Email Sequences
    description: Multi-step email sequences with enrollment
  - name: Conversations
    description: Threaded conversation view per contact
  - name: Automations
    description: Workflow automations (native + n8n), publishing, analytics
  - name: Automation Executions
    description: Automation execution logs and step details
  - name: Workflows
    description: Simple trigger-action workflows
  - name: Drip Campaigns
    description: SMS drip campaign engine
  - name: Custom Fields
    description: Custom field definitions for contacts and deals
  - name: Calendars
    description: Internal calendar and appointment management
  - name: Calendar Connections
    description: Google / Microsoft calendar sync
  - name: Booking Pages
    description: Public booking pages (Calendly-style)
  - name: Appointments
    description: Appointment scheduling
  - name: Forms
    description: Lead capture forms and submissions
  - name: Invoices
    description: Invoice creation, sending, payments, PDF generation
  - name: Products
    description: Product catalog for invoices
  - name: Notifications
    description: In-app notifications
  - name: Files
    description: File uploads and attachments
  - name: API Keys
    description: API key management
  - name: Users
    description: Team member management and invitations
  - name: Settings
    description: Account settings, branding, SMS/Twilio configuration
  - name: Billing
    description: Stripe billing, checkout, and subscription status
  - name: Webhooks
    description: Outbound webhook management and logs
  - name: Integrations
    description: Third-party integrations (Zapier, etc.)
  - name: Reports
    description: Pipeline, revenue, activity, team, and custom reports
  - name: Search
    description: Global search across contacts, companies, deals
  - name: Bulk Operations
    description: Bulk update, delete, and tag contacts and deals
  - name: Imports
    description: CSV import jobs with mapping and deduplication
  - name: Smart Lists
    description: Static contact lists
  - name: Lead Routing
    description: Lead assignment routing rules and assignment history
  - name: Scoring Rules
    description: Lead scoring rule management
  - name: Document Templates
    description: Proposal and contract templates with merge fields
  - name: Email Domains
    description: Custom email domain verification (Resend)
  - name: Dialer
    description: Click-to-call dialer via Twilio
  - name: Calls
    description: Call log management
  - name: Chat
    description: Internal team chat channels and messages
  - name: Push Notifications
    description: Web push subscription management
  - name: Dashboard
    description: Dashboard summary metrics
  - name: AI
    description: AI-powered features (chat, email compose, contact enrichment)
  - name: Admin
    description: Super-admin account management and impersonation
  - name: Public
    description: Unauthenticated public endpoints (booking, form submit)

security:
  - BearerAuth: []

paths:
  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Auth
  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  /auth/register:
    post:
      operationId: register
      summary: Register a new account
      description: Creates a new user and account. Rate limited to 3 requests per hour per IP.
      tags:
        - Auth
      security: []
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              type: object
              required:
                - email
                - password
                - accountName
              properties:
                email:
                  type: string
                  format: email
                  maxLength: 254
                password:
                  type: string
                  minLength: 8
                firstName:
                  type: string
                lastName:
                  type: string
                accountName:
                  type: string
                  minLength: 2
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Registration successful
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/AuthResponse"
        "400":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest"
        "429":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited"
      parameters: []

  /auth/login:
    post:
      operationId: login
      summary: Log in with email and password
      description: Authenticates user credentials and returns a session cookie. Rate limited to 5 requests per 15 minutes per IP.
      tags:
        - Auth
      security: []
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              type: object
              required:
                - email
                - password
              properties:
                email:
                  type: string
                  format: email
                password:
                  type: string
                accountId:
                  type: string
                  format: uuid
                  description: Target account ID (optional, defaults to first account)
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Login successful
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/AuthResponse"
        "401":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
        "429":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited"
      parameters: []

  /auth/logout:
    post:
      operationId: logout
      summary: Log out (destroy session)
      tags:
        - Auth
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Logged out successfully
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataEnvelope"
      parameters: []

  /auth/me:
    get:
      operationId: getMe
      summary: Get current authenticated user
      description: Identical to GET /users/me, byte for byte (that route re-exports this handler) — including `data.account.name`.
      tags:
        - Auth
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Current user and account info.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                properties:
                  data:
                    $ref: "#/components/schemas/MeResponseData"
        "401":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
        "403":
          description: "An API-key caller only: the key (or an ancestor in its lineage) denies this request — an IP outside the key's allowlist, a method its tier doesn't allow, a scope it lacks, or a child key that is unrestricted or missing an ancestor's explicit-only grant. Never returned for a browser session."
        "429":
          description: An API-key caller only — the key's own rate limit, or its lineage-wide rate limit, is exceeded. Never returned for a browser session.
        "500":
          description: Internal server error.
      parameters: []

  /auth/change-password:
    post:
      operationId: changePassword
      summary: Change password (authenticated)
      tags:
        - Auth
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              type: object
              required:
                - currentPassword
                - newPassword
              properties:
                currentPassword:
                  type: string
                newPassword:
                  type: string
                  minLength: 8
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Password changed
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataEnvelope"
        "400":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest"
        "401":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
      parameters: []

  /auth/forgot-password:
    post:
      operationId: forgotPassword
      summary: Request a password reset email
      tags:
        - Auth
      security: []
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              type: object
              required:
                - email
              properties:
                email:
                  type: string
                  format: email
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Reset email sent (always returns 200 to prevent email enumeration)
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataEnvelope"
      parameters: []

  /auth/reset-password:
    post:
      operationId: resetPassword
      summary: Reset password with token
      tags:
        - Auth
      security: []
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              type: object
              required:
                - token
                - password
              properties:
                token:
                  type: string
                password:
                  type: string
                  minLength: 8
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Password reset successful
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataEnvelope"
        "400":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest"
      parameters: []

  /auth/switch-account:
    post:
      operationId: switchAccount
      summary: Switch to a different account
      tags:
        - Auth
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              type: object
              required:
                - accountId
              properties:
                accountId:
                  type: string
                  format: uuid
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Account switched successfully
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataEnvelope"
        "403":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
      parameters: []

  /auth/accept-invite:
    post:
      operationId: acceptInvite
      summary: Accept a team invitation
      tags:
        - Auth
      security: []
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              type: object
              required:
                - token
                - password
              properties:
                token:
                  type: string
                password:
                  type: string
                  minLength: 8
                firstName:
                  type: string
                lastName:
                  type: string
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Invite accepted, session created
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataEnvelope"
        "400":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest"
      parameters: []

  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Contacts
  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  /contacts:
    get:
      operationId: listContacts
      summary: List contacts
      description: |
        Returns a paginated list of contacts. Supports search, filtering by tag,
        source, company, assigned user, date ranges, lead score, and smart views.

        Smart views: `needs_follow_up`, `hot_leads`, `new_this_week`,
        `recently_won`, `untagged`, `missing_email`, `missing_phone`.
      tags:
        - Contacts
      parameters:
        - name: assigned_to
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: cf
          in: query
          required: false
          description: string — compact custom-field filters for generated clients. Use fieldKey=value pairs (comma-separated) or a JSON object; values can be exact, __notempty__, or __empty__.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: company
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: company_id
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: created_from
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: created_to
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: deal_context_owners
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: deal_context_stages
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: deal_context_statuses
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: email
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Exact email lookup, repeatable (?email=a@x.com&email=b@y.com; form style, exploded). Each value is trimmed and lower-cased, must be a valid address of at most 254 characters, and matches the contact's primary email or any secondary email slot (email_2 and up). Duplicates collapse; at most 20 distinct addresses. An invalid or empty value, or more than 20 distinct addresses, is a 400. Combines with every other filter (AND), inside the caller's account and visibility. Accounts whose identifier index is still being built answer from a slower lookup; if the stored spellings of the requested addresses exceed that lookup's bind budget (a count of spellings, not of contacts, and other filters do not reduce it), the answer is a 422 until the identifier backfill completes.
          style: form
          explode: true
          schema:
            type: array
            items:
              type: string
            uniqueItems: false
        - name: exclude_master_status
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: filters
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: import_id
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: include
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: limit
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: integer
            default: 50
            minimum: 1
            maximum: 200
          x-default-provenance: handler_literal
        - name: master_status
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: min_score
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: integer
        - name: order
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: page
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Page number
          schema:
            type: integer
            default: 1
            minimum: 1
            maximum: 1000000
          x-default-provenance: handler_literal
        - name: per_page
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Items per page (max 200)
          schema:
            type: integer
            default: 50
            minimum: 1
            maximum: 200
          x-default-provenance: handler_literal
        - name: reachability
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: search
          in: query
          required: false
          description: "Text search over name, email, phone (any formatting, incl. secondary phones) and company. A Lead ID (8 to 32 hex characters of a contact id or of one of its deals' ids, dashes optional, any case; a whole id matches exactly) resolves by id first: when it holds a hex letter and names a contact you can see, or one owning a deal you can see, the result is those contacts only; when it names none it falls back to the text search. A digits-only Lead ID (also a phone fragment) returns the text and phone matches plus the id matches."
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: smart_view
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: smartListId
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: sort
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: source
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: tag
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: tags
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: updated_from
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: updated_to
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Query parameter read by this route.
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: cf[<key>]
          in: query
          required: false
          description: string — filter by contact custom field key. Use an exact value, __notempty__, or __empty__; key must match a contact custom-field definition for the account.
          schema:
            type: string
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Paginated list of contacts
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/PaginatedResponse"
        "401":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
    post:
      operationId: createContact
      summary: Create a contact
      description: "Creates a new contact. Rate limited to 30 requests per minute. With `callId` (the unknown-caller prompt's \"Create new lead\"), the new contact is linked to that contact-less INBOUND call in the SAME transaction: the phone is the call's own caller number (a submitted `phone` must be omitted or strictly the same number, else 422 `phone_not_call_number`), stored under the account's country; `firstName` is required (400 `first_name_required`) and, for this lead only, the account's form-required contact fields and required custom fields are not required (values that are sent are still validated). The caller needs `dialer.create` (an API key also needs the `calls` scope; a `dialer` key covers it). A call that does not exist is 404 `call_not_found`; a call already linked is 409 `call_already_linked` (or 404 `call_not_found` when its contact is hidden from the caller); an outbound call is 422 `call_not_inbound`; a call with no usable caller number is 422 `number_unusable`. The lead's `source` (always \"Inbound Call\") and owner are derived from the call, so a request with `callId` must NOT carry `source` or `assignedTo` (any value, null included): it is refused with 422 `call_derived_fields`. Nothing is created on any refusal. callId derives the owner: the call taker, else the signed-in session user; an API-key request, an inactive call taker or an inactive fallback user derive no owner. A contact that derives no owner is then subject to the workspace's normal lead routing and Smart View assignment like any other create, so it may still end up assigned."
      tags:
        - Contacts
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              allOf:
                - $ref: "#/components/schemas/ContactCreate"
                - type: object
                  properties:
                    callId:
                      type: string
                      format: uuid
                      nullable: true
                      description: "A contact-less inbound call to link the new contact to, in the same transaction (board #35, the unknown-caller prompt). When set, `source` and `assignedTo` must be omitted: both are derived from the call (422 `call_derived_fields`). callId derives the owner: the call taker, else the signed-in session user; an API-key request, an inactive call taker or an inactive fallback user derive no owner. A contact that derives no owner is then subject to the workspace's normal lead routing and Smart View assignment like any other create, so it may still end up assigned."
            examples:
              createAndLink:
                summary: Create a lead from an unknown inbound call and link the call
                value:
                  firstName: Carla
                  lastName: Diaz
                  callId: 9b2d7c1a-5e4f-4a3b-9c8d-7e6f5a4b3c2d
      responses:
        "201":
          description: Contact created
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataEnvelope"
        "400":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest"
        "402":
          description: Trial expired or contact limit reached
        "409":
          description: 'The person already exists (identity rules R1 to R4, matched on email or phone confirmed by name) or (with `callId`) the call is already linked (`call_already_linked`); nothing is created. The identity 409 answers `error`, `existingId`, `rule`, `ruleVersion`, `matchedOn` and `reason`; `reason` says to update the existing record instead. The refusal is recorded after the fact: one value-free identity ledger row (outcome `refused_existing`, door `api`), keyed by a one-way digest of the Idempotency-Key or the request id (the header value itself is never stored) together with the decision, so an identical retry writes nothing new and a changed decision writes a new row. When the decision identified a same-name record pair, `reason` says so ("The identity decision also identified a same-name record pair (<rule>)."); that sentence does not say whether the pair was recorded.'
        "413":
          description: Custom fields payload too large
        "422":
          description: (with `callId`) `call_not_inbound`, `number_unusable`, `phone_not_call_number`, or `call_derived_fields` (the request also carried `source` or `assignedTo`, which are derived from the call); nothing is created
        "429":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/RateLimited"
      parameters:
        - name: Idempotency-Key
          in: header
          required: false
          description: "Optional: one key per creation attempt (1-255 printable ASCII characters, not blank), reused only to retry the SAME request. Same key + same request body replays the original response (Idempotent-Replay: true); same key + a different body is refused with 422. Two DISTINCT 409s under this key, never interchangeable: (1) the ORIGINAL attempt is still being processed — wait for the Retry-After seconds given, then retry with the SAME key; (2) the key was already SPENT by a prior attempt that failed or has an unknown outcome (code idempotency_key_spent) — verify whether that attempt took effect BEFORE sending a brand-new key; resending the SAME key here only replays this 409 again, it never re-runs the request. If the wrapper's OWN write to RELEASE a failed attempt's claim cannot be confirmed, the SAME key instead answers 503 idempotency_claim_held until the held claim expires — retry with a NEW key, never the same one. If the wrapper's OWN write to confirm a SUCCESSFUL completion cannot be confirmed, the mutation may have gone through anyway: the SAME key instead answers 503 idempotency_outcome_unknown — verify the outcome before any new-key retry, exactly as case (2) above. A blank or malformed key is refused with 400 idempotency_key_invalid, on dry_run requests too (a dry run never records the key)."
          schema:
            type: string
            pattern: ^[!-~](?:[ -~]{0,253}[!-~])?$
        - name: dry_run
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Validate the mutation without persisting changes.
          schema:
            type: boolean
        - name: sandbox
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Run the mutation in sandbox mode.
          schema:
            type: boolean

  /contacts/{id}:
    get:
      operationId: getContact
      summary: Get a contact by ID
      tags:
        - Contacts
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/IdParam"
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Contact details
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                properties:
                  data:
                    $ref: "#/components/schemas/ContactRead"
        "404":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound"
    patch:
      operationId: updateContact
      summary: Update a contact
      description: "Deprecated on contacts (2026-10-13): `customFields.oes_number` and `customFields.dpp_oes_raw`. The OES number identifies an opportunity, so it lives on the deal card (deal custom fields `oes_number` / `dpp_oes_raw`, one live card per number: PATCH /deals/{id}). The contact keys are still accepted (and kept unique per workspace) while existing contact values are migrated onto their cards; new integrations should write the card."
      tags:
        - Contacts
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/IdParam"
        - name: dry_run
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Validate the mutation without persisting changes.
          schema:
            type: boolean
        - name: sandbox
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Run the mutation in sandbox mode.
          schema:
            type: boolean
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: "#/components/schemas/ContactUpdate"
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Contact updated
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataEnvelope"
        "400":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/BadRequest"
        "404":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound"
        "409":
          description: 'Nothing was written. With `code: "contact_changed"` the contact changed after the revision the caller pinned in `expectedRevision`: `revision` is its current revision and `contact` the contact as it is stored now (the shape a successful PATCH returns); read it, then retry with the new `revision`. With `code: "oes_number_taken"` the `customFields.oes_number` submitted is already on another live contact in the workspace (compared by its digits, 6 or more): `error` names that contact (name and id) only when the caller may see it, otherwise it is the generic line "another contact in this workspace already has this OES #"; a `dry_run` always answers the generic line. Other 409s without a code (an already-set custom field, a duplicate email or phone, a required custom field cleared meanwhile) are described by `error`.'
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - error
                properties:
                  error:
                    type: string
                  code:
                    type: string
                    enum:
                      - contact_changed
                      - oes_number_taken
                  revision:
                    type: integer
                  contact:
                    type: object
    delete:
      operationId: deleteContact
      summary: Soft-delete a contact
      tags:
        - Contacts
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/IdParam"
        - name: dry_run
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Validate the mutation without persisting changes.
          schema:
            type: boolean
        - name: sandbox
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Run the mutation in sandbox mode.
          schema:
            type: boolean
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Contact deleted
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/DataEnvelope"
        "404":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/NotFound"

