  /sms-providers/options:
    get:
      operationId: getSmsProvidersOptions
      summary: List sms-providers options
      description: |
        Provider picker for the SMS provider dropdown: the id and name of every provider the send service can
        actually use (active webhook providers whose webhook URL passes the outbound safety check), ordered by
        name. Reachable with a key scoped `sms` or `messages`; the caller needs communications.view or
        communications.create.

        Pagination on this operation is cursor-based and differs from the global `page` / `per_page` rules:
        - `limit` (1-50, default 50) is how many providers to return. A `limit` above 50 is capped to 50, not
          rejected; 0, a negative or non-integer value, or a repeated `limit` is a 400.
        - `cursor` resumes after the last row the previous page scanned. Pass `meta.nextCursor` back unchanged.
          An empty, malformed or repeated cursor is a 400.
        - One request checks at most 250 providers, so a page can hold fewer than `limit` items while more
          remain. Keep paging while `meta.nextCursor` is not null; `meta.truncated` is true exactly when it is set.

        A 503 with `Retry-After` means the webhook URLs could not be verified right now (a resolver outage);
        the response is never a partial list.
      tags:
        - Sms Providers
      parameters:
        - name: cursor
          in: query
          required: false
          description: "string — opaque continuation token: pass the previous page's meta.nextCursor unchanged to resume after the last row it scanned. Omit for the first page; an empty, malformed or repeated cursor is a 400."
          schema:
            type: string
        - name: limit
          in: query
          required: false
          description: integer 1-50 (default 50) — how many usable providers to return. A value above 50 is capped to 50 (not rejected); 0, a negative or non-integer value, or a repeated limit is a 400.
          schema:
            type: integer
            minimum: 1
            maximum: 50
            default: 50
          x-default-provenance: authored_operation
      responses:
        "200":
          description: One page of usable providers
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - data
                  - meta
                properties:
                  data:
                    type: array
                    items:
                      type: object
                      required:
                        - id
                        - name
                      properties:
                        id:
                          type: string
                          format: uuid
                        name:
                          type: string
                  meta:
                    type: object
                    required:
                      - nextCursor
                      - truncated
                    properties:
                      nextCursor:
                        type: string
                        nullable: true
                        description: Opaque token for the next page (pass as `cursor`); null when every provider has been scanned
                      truncated:
                        type: boolean
                        description: True exactly when nextCursor is set, i.e. more providers remain to be scanned
        "400":
          description: Invalid cursor or limit (the error names which)
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
        "401":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
        "403":
          $ref: "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
        "503":
          description: Provider webhook URLs could not be verified right now; retry after the Retry-After seconds
          headers:
            Retry-After:
              schema:
                type: integer
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
